<title>ITALY: Specialists bid for one bln lire of Italy Cct.</title>
<headline>Specialists bid for one bln lire of Italy Cct.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Specialist bond traders bid for one billion lire of 10-year fixed-rate bonds (BTP) against the Italian Treasury's offer of 200 billion lire of paper.</p>
<p>Earlier, the Treasury received bids for 2.985 trillion lire at the open auction for the February 1, 2007 paper, against two trillion lire worth of certificates on offer.</p>
<p>The auction price was set at 98.60 from 98.40 at the previous BTP sale at the end of January.</p>
</text>
